All local gates pass on the first implementation. The certificate language has about \(1.7\times10^{10}\) structure-aware candidates at \(d=16\), the demo has exactly 24 valid affine relabellings, all four attacks fail 0/8, and the compact decoder takes at most 204 packed exact operations. The important open question is now empirical: the full route is only about 1,000 packed operations at the initial rung, so the oracle loop—not cardinality—will decide whether this is a meaningful Track B benchmark.
