codex
The failure is a one-dimensional spectral degeneracy, not a solved attack: seven seeds had the expected 3D \(-1\) eigenspace and one had dimension 4. In the 4D case, vertices in the same true fibre differ only along one projective nuisance direction. I’m strengthening the exact spectral decoder to identify that most-repeated direction and quotient it out before fitting the affine certificate; this remains a graph-spectral reference algorithm and does not use the planted answer.
